    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5ee6b2b9_53d4dc2f",
        "filename": "core/java/android/os/Parcel.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 521,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-03T04:11:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, then I think we need to be more explicit. I don\u0027t have an exact javadoc description, but I think the following should be mentioned:\n\nA) calling this prevents you from sending the same parcel to other binder objects\nB) in order to be future proof, you need to call this whenever you send a parcel over to ANY binder\nC) the generated code from AIDL compiler is already using this\nD) if you call this multiple times with different `binder` arguments, then the association is made only with the last binder object\n\nI wish we could enforce (B) for the clients targeting T or beyond.\n\nI also see that there is no way to cut the association.",
      "parentUuid": "4dd3411f_5f12b601",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 521,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 521,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "92ab137b56b59fa582032dfdf956d85dde9b02df",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
